     "text": "{\"count\": 0, \"rationale\": \"No single non-foothold, non-target step is a chokepoint, because there are at least two independent routes to crownData:exfiltrate. Route 1: kerberoast:credentialAccess (from wifiGuest or vpnGateway) leads to backupHost:lateralMovement, then codeRepo:collection, then crownData. Route 2: mailClient:execution leads to tokenCache:credentialAccess. memoryDump:credentialAccess comes from supplychain. Both feed rdpLogin:authenticate (AND), which leads to printServer:lateralMovement, then shareMount:collection, then crownData. The two routes share no intermediate step, so blocking any one step leaves the other route open. A third route also exists: workstation, browserStore and tokenCache lead to dbLogin, then jumpHost, then dbReplica, then crownData.\"}"
    }
   ],
